---
title: Tomato sauce with onion and butter
servings: 6
tags: [italian, vegetarian, make-ahead]
cuisine: italian
time: 1 hour
source: Marcella Hazan's Tomato Sauce with Onion and Butter by Marcella Hazan, from Essentials of Classic Italian Cooking, via PBS Food, https://www.pbs.org/food/recipes/marcella-hazans-tomato-sauce-with-onion-and-butter
---

Put the @tomatoes{2%lb}(ripe, peeled and cut up), @unsalted butter{5%tbsp},
@yellow onion{1}(peeled and halved) and a little @salt{} in a #saucepan{}.

Cook uncovered at a very slow, steady simmer ~{45%minutes}, until the butter
separates from the tomatoes. Stir now and then, crushing any big pieces against
the side of the pan.

Taste for salt and take out the onion. Toss with @pasta{1%lb} and serve with
@parmesan{}(Parmigiano-Reggiano, freshly grated).

> Out of season, use 2 cups of canned Italian plum tomatoes, cut up, with their
> juice. To peel fresh tomatoes, drop them into boiling water for a minute and
> the skins slip off.
